{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Implement acceptance tests as black-box, end-to-end tests that run each module as a Spring Cloud Stream application and verify message flow through a real binder (RabbitMQ/Kafka) provisioned with Testcontainers.",
    "Use Java 17 with Spring Framework 6 / Spring Boot 3 baseline as mandated by the specification, with JUnit 5 as the test framework.",
    "External service dependencies are containerized via Testcontainers: GreenMail for the Mail source, an SFTP server image (e.g., atmoz/sftp) for the SFTP source, and Redis for the aggregator processor's message store; reactor-ip and reactor-syslog tests use embedded Netty-based client/sender utilities; http-client tests use WireMock to stub HTTP endpoints.",
    "Create a shared acceptance-test base infrastructure (abstract test class, container lifecycle management, binder configuration helpers, reusable assertion utilities) to be reused across all 8 module test suites.",
    "Acceptance tests are placed in a dedicated source set/module executed by the Maven Failsafe (or equivalent Gradle) plugin in a separate 'acceptance-test' stage so they run on every CI build without slowing unit-test phases.",
    "The bridge processor test is a simple binder-to-binder passthrough verification and requires no external containers beyond the binder."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "All 8 modules (Mail, reactor-ip, reactor-syslog, SFTP sources; aggregator, analytic-pmml, bridge, http-client processors) already exist, compile, and have passing unit tests; this increment adds acceptance test coverage only, with no feature changes.",
    "A CI system (e.g., GitHub Actions or Jenkins) already exists and its build agents support Docker, which is required by Testcontainers.",
    "A sample PMML model file and representative input/output data for analytic-pmml are available or can be created quickly from existing documentation.",
    "Effort estimates include test design, fixture/test-data creation, implementation, debugging of flaky container startup/timing issues, and one round of code review rework; all work is performed by a single developer.",
    "Only one binder variant (e.g., RabbitMQ) is exercised per module in acceptance tests; multi-binder matrices are out of scope.",
    "No changes to module production code are needed beyond minor testability adjustments, which are included in the per-module estimates."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Analyze modules and define acceptance test strategy",
      "activity_description": "Review the 8 modules' configurations and contracts, define the black-box acceptance test approach, select binder and container strategy, and enumerate test scenarios per module.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Build shared acceptance test infrastructure",
      "activity_description": "Implement the shared base test class, Testcontainers lifecycle management for the binder, common assertion/wait utilities, build plugin configuration (Failsafe/Gradle task), and the CI test stage wiring.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Mail source acceptance tests (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Stand up a GreenMail container, send test emails, and verify the Mail source emits expected messages (headers, body, attachments) to the binder, including polling and error cases.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "reactor-ip source acceptance tests (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Implement TCP/UDP client senders against the running reactor-ip source and verify received datagrams/messages are published to the binder with correct framing and decoding.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "reactor-syslog source acceptance tests (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Create a syslog message sender (UDP/TCP) producing RFC 3164/5424 messages and verify the reactor-syslog source parses and publishes them correctly, including malformed message handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 14
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "SFTP source acceptance tests (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Provision a containerized SFTP server with seeded directories/files and credentials, and verify file pickup, local synchronization, filtering, and message emission to the binder.",
      "most_likely_effort": 14
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "aggregator processor acceptance tests (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Configure a Redis-backed message store in a container and verify correlation, aggregation, release strategies (count/timeout), and state handling by sending message sequences through the binder.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "analytic-pmml processor acceptance tests (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Load a sample PMML model, send input tuples through the processor, and verify evaluated model outputs are emitted correctly, including invalid input handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "bridge processor acceptance tests (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Verify end-to-end passthrough bridging from the input binding to the output binding, confirming message content and headers are preserved.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "http-client processor acceptance tests (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Stub HTTP endpoints with WireMock, send request messages through the processor, and verify HTTP method, headers, body mapping, and response/reply emission, including error status handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "CI integration, stabilization, and flaky test remediation",
      "activity_description": "Run the full acceptance suite in the CI pipeline, tune container startup timeouts and waits, fix flaky tests, and confirm the suite gates every build as required.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Documentation, code review, and rework",
      "activity_description": "Document how to run the acceptance tests locally and in CI, address review feedback across all test suites, and finalize the increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 136
  }
}
```

